    <statement><p>Determine whether the series converges, and if so find its sum.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle \sum_{k=1}^{\infty} \frac{2^{k+4}}{9^{k-1}} =</m> <fillin characters="50" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>(Enter DNE if the sum does not exist.)</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{9\cdot 2^{4+1}}{9^{-1+1}\mathopen{}\left(9-2\right)}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>a=32</m> and <m>r={\frac{2}{9}}</m>, <m>|r|\lt 1</m> so 


<m>\displaystyle \sum_{k=1}^{\infty} \frac{2^{k+4}}{9^{k-1}} =32 \sum_{k=0}^{\infty} \left({\frac{2}{9}}\right)^{k} =\frac{32}{1-\left({\frac{2}{9}}\right)}={\frac{288}{7}}</m>


</solution>
